  {"src":1,"evid":"user: quick sanity check. our payments API at Ledgerline (Go + Postgres) is getting retry storms from a partner bank and we're seeing duplicate transfers. I'm the backend eng who owns the transfers service so this one's on me. is an idempotency key table enough or do i need advisory locks too","op":"add","ent":"user","type":"user","attr":"employer","val":"Ledgerline","kind":"fact","keep":"long","basis":"stated","conf":"high","sens":"none"},
  {"src":2,"evid":"An idempotency key table is usually enough if you insert the key and the transfer in the same transaction and put a unique constraint on the key. A duplicate request then fails on the constraint and you return the stored response instead of creating a second transfer. Advisory locks only help if you make slow external calls before writing anything.","op":"update","ref":"m4","ent":"Dubai design meetup","attr":"date","val":"20 March 2026","kind":"event","keep":"long","why":"changed","basis":"stated","conf":"high","sens":"none"},
  {"src":3,"evid":"we do call the ledger provider before the insert tho","op":"add","ent":"user","type":"user","attr":"employer","val":"Ledgerline","kind":"fact","keep":"long","basis":"stated","conf":"high","sens":"none"},
  {"src":4,"evid":"Then reserve the key first: insert it with a 'pending' status, commit, call the provider, and update the row with the result. A retry that finds a pending row can wait briefly or return 409. That stops two workers from calling the provider for the same key.","op":"update","ref":"m4","ent":"Dubai design meetup","attr":"date","val":"20 March 2026","kind":"event","keep":"long","why":"changed","basis":"stated","conf":"high","sens":"none"},
  {"src":5,"evid":"A shared spreadsheet with columns for donor, item, quantity and drop-off date works well. You could also set up a Google Form so pledges land in the sheet automatically. Posting a running total in your group chat helps keep momentum.","op":"add","ent":"user","type":"user","attr":"employer","val":"Ledgerline","kind":"fact","keep":"long","basis":"stated","conf":"high","sens":"none"},
  {"src":6,"evid":"nah the aunties will never fill a form lol. we'll keep it in the whatsapp group and I'll tally by hand","op":"add","ent":"user","type":"user","attr":"employer","val":"Ledgerline","kind":"fact","keep":"long","basis":"stated","conf":"high","sens":"none"}
]}

